From 9b9107c0fd323188a3a0e2092927d74eb330d11e Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Sergey Fedorov <barracuda@macos-powerpc.org>
Date: Mon, 5 Oct 2026 16:19:22 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 65/65] minicargo: expand glob patterns in a virtual
 workspace's member list

Member selection for a virtual workspace root skipped any `members`
entry containing `*`, so a workspace that lists its members only by
pattern had no candidates at all. jql 9.0.3 has

    [workspace]
    members = ["crates/*"]

and failed with

    Virtual workspace root - unable to pick a member to build. Members:
    EXCEPTION: Virtual workspace root: pass `--package <name>` to select a member

Expand a pattern in the last path component against the entries of its
parent directory (`*` and `?`, as cargo's glob does), sorted for
a stable order; entries without a `Cargo.toml` are dropped by the existing
check. A wildcard in a directory component is still unsupported and now
warns. The selection heuristics are unchanged: for `jql-9.0.3` the
member named like the directory (`jql`) is chosen, and `--package`
still overrides.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 tools/minicargo/main.cpp | 84 +++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++-
 1 file changed, 82 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

